 "_evidence": "Lower-case map at 0x833e18 as the game builds it: 0x0054d70c stores, for al = 0..255, the result of the thunk 0x5a4972 = user32!CharLowerA(al) (a char argument with a zero high word, so CharLowerA converts that one character). The image holds zeros (filled at start-up), so routines that compare folded characters (0x0052f578 matches '.' after a device name, folded NUL) need the real map: A-Z -> a-z and, for the Windows-1252 ANSI code page, 0x8a/0x8c/0x8e -> +0x10, 0x9f -> 0xff, 0xc0..0xde except 0xd7 -> +0x20; every other byte maps to itself. One field per byte (a single value each) because identity runs cannot share one value set.",
